{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' run.sh\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n# lanes: codex           Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n#        kimi            Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n#        codex-sandboxed Codex CLI executed inside sandbox/agent.sb (isolated HOME), with output written to a temporary location and copied back after the sandbox exits\nset -u\nD=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nT=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\nR=\"$D/runs/$T-$A-r$REP\"; rm -rf \"$R\"; mkdir -p \"$R\"\nW=$(mktemp -d /tmp/h-XXXXXX); cp -R \"$D/tasks/$T/.\" \"$W/\"\nP=\"$(cat \"$D/tasks/$T.prompt\")\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$P\" > \"$R/prompt.txt\"\nTO=1200\n\ncodex_run() {\n  ( cd \"$W\" && timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n      -o \"$R/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n}\n\n# Codex run inside the same sandbox used for the kimi lane. The sandbox profile denies\n# read/write access to the real HOME, so we give the agent a temporary HOME and write\n# the final answer to a scratch directory inside /tmp. After sandbox‑exec returns we\n# copy the result into the run folder.\ncodex_sandboxed_run() {\n  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH SCRATCH\n  SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n  SCRATCH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/codex-sb-XXXXXX)\n  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n      timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n      -o \"$SCRATCH/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n  local rc=$?\n  # copy final answer out of the sandbox if it exists\n  if [ -f \"$SCRATCH/final.txt\" ]; then\n    cp \"$SCRATCH/final.txt\" \"$R/final.txt\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$SH\" \"$SCRATCH\"\n  return $rc\n}\n\n# Kimi's output goes to Moonshot: its shell runs under sandbox/agent.sb with an empty scratch HOME.\nkimi_run() {\n  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n      env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n      < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n  local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n}\n\nstart=$(date +%s)\ncase $A in\n  codex) codex_run;;\n  codex-sandboxed) codex_sandboxed_run;;\n  kimi)  kimi_run;;\n  *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\nesac\nrc=$?\nend=$(date +%s)\necho \"{\\\"task\\\":\\\"$T\\\",\\\"lane\\\":\\\"$A\\\",\\\"rep\\\":$REP,\\\"exit_code\\\":$rc,\\\"wall_s\\\":$((end-start))}\" > \"$R/meta.json\"\npython3 \"$D/check_answer.py\" \"$R\" > \"$R/answer.json\"\nrm -rf \"$W\"\necho \"$T-$A-r$REP rc=$rc answer=$(python3 -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('$R/answer.json'))['final']))\" 2>/dev/null) chars\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"**What was added**\n- Added a new lane `codex-sandboxed` to `run.sh`.\n- Implemented `codex_sandboxed_run` that mirrors the unsandboxed `codex` run but executes inside `sandbox/agent.sb`.\n- Created temporary `HOME` (`SH`) and scratch output directory (`SCRATCH`) in `/tmp`.\n- Directed Codex’s `-o` output to `$SCRATCH/final.txt` inside the sandbox, then copied it to the run folder after `sandbox-exec` finishes.\n- Cleaned up temporary directories and returned the original exit code.\n- Updated the case statement to handle `codex-sandboxed`.\n\n**Parts of the colleague’s note that applied**\n1. **Write output to a scratch folder in `/tmp`** – used `$SCRATCH` for the final answer file.\n2. **Copy the result after `sandbox‑exec` returns** – copied `final.txt` from the scratch folder back to the run folder.\n3. **Keep stdout/stderr redirection unchanged** – `agent.log` and `agent.err` are still written directly to the run folder.\n\n**What was ignored**\n- Log checking for “Operation not permitted” – not needed for the lane implementation.\n- Specific Mistral Vibe references – the fix is generic and only applied to Codex."}}
